KeywordAbility(
    name: "offspring",
    params: [Cost],
    spelling: "offspring",
    grammar: FixedKeyword(
        surface: "offspring",
    ),
    // STOP. "Offspring [cost]" means "You may pay an additional [cost] as you cast
    // this spell" and "When this permanent ENTERS, if its offspring cost was paid,
    // create a token that's a copy of it, except it's 1/1." [CR#702.175a] Both halves
    // are writable — `StaticSpec::AddedCost` and an enters trigger reading
    // `Paid(Readback(ByKeyword("Offspring")))` — but the pair cannot stand together:
    // `keywordBodyPartFits` requires every TRIGGERED part of a definition to key on
    // the keyword's own stack regime, and offspring's registry row is
    // `regime: AtCasting` because its first ability functions on the stack. Written
    // out, `Intrepid Rabbit` refuses with `[Semantics.Refusal.keywordBodyFits
    // "Offspring"]`: the enters event's regime is `none`. Clearing the row's regime
    // to satisfy the second ability would misdescribe the first, so the definition
    // waits on the law admitting a keyword whose two abilities function in different
    // zones (squad has the same shape).
    body: Keyword(keyword: "Offspring", params: [Cost(cost: Param(0))], body: []),
)
